trial: halve phrase-medial nucleus durations

DIAGNOSTIC, not a fix: phrase_medial_dur scales one class of nuclei by
75/100; this tries 75/150 so all mid-phrase nuclei come out clearly
shorter. If the word-final -ie emphasis vanishes among the rushing,
duration through this path is confirmed and the factor gets tuned for
real. If the -ie still sticks out, the cause is elsewhere (another
duration path, or pitch/energy) and this reverts.
Applied at build time so CI builds the same tree.
diff --git a/lang/enus/rules/es_ndur.dr b/lang/enus/rules/es_ndur.dr
index f6e9e6f..478c74f 100644
--- a/lang/enus/rules/es_ndur.dr
+++ b/lang/enus/rules/es_ndur.dr
@@ -3434,7 +3434,7 @@ label L4 was $X8$99871
   addk 2788 reg r6 into r1
   load movl ind reg r1 0 into r0
   mul imull imm 75 reg r0 into r0
-  push imm 100
+  push imm 150
   widen cltd
   popreg r7
   div idivl reg r7
